proof.text:
Now let $F$ be any étale $B$-module sheaf. Constructible approximation writes $F=\varinjlim_{\alpha\in I}F_\alpha$ for a small filtered diagram of constructible $B$-module sheaves; its hypotheses hold because $T$ is qcqs and $B$ is finite. Comparison inverse image is a left adjoint on module sheaves, the finite-coefficient encoding is an equivalence, and scalar restriction preserves colimits by the coextension adjunction. Consequently $\operatorname{Res}
u_T^*F=\varinjlim_\alpha\operatorname{Res}
u_T^*F_\alpha$, with the actual induced linear maps. Put this diagram in degree zero. It is a strict small filtered diagram with common termwise lower bound $0$, whose members lie in the hull by step 4. Its termwise colimit is the displayed sheaf in degree zero. The specified filtered-colimit closure proves $\operatorname{Res}
u_T^*F[0]\in\mathcal G_T(R^c)$ without any finiteness assertion about $F$.
